{% extends "ap2_en.j2" %}

{% block summary %}
<p>The OSLO-Person application profile brings together terms from vocabularies about people and mainly from the <a href="/ns/persoon">OSLO-Person vocabulary</a>.</p>
<p>In principle, an application profile has a specific application in mind, and for that purpose, additional constraints are imposed, such as cardinalities and prescribed code lists. That is not the case here, so we speak of a basic profile. It contains the information that is considered relevant within OSLO for exchanging data about people. That does not change the fact that the profile brings together terms that we mainly see in the context of a population register.</p>
<p>The profile includes terms related to the identification of a person (name, gender, date of birth) but also terms that describe the civil characteristics of persons (personal relationships such as marriage, family, and relations with the state such as citizenship and residence/domicile). For more details, we refer to the OSLO Person vocabulary.</p>
<p>The profile imposes minimal restrictions; only the data that identifies the person is mandatory. There are currently no prescribed code lists.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block status %}
<p>This application profile is intended to clarify the specific use of entities relevant to the described application.</p>
<p>This document was published as a Candidate Standard. The specification as described in this document is currently undergoing a period of public review, during which no changes to this specification will be made.<br/>This document is intended to become a standard in the described domain. Nevertheless, it currently has no official status and does not represent consensus within OSLO.</p>
{% endblock %}

{% block conformance %}
<p>An application profile is a data exchange specification that introduces additional restrictions for applying vocabulary. 
Such additional restrictions may include the following elements:</p>
<p>
<ul>
<li>refinement of terminology (classes and properties) consistent with the semantics from the relevant specifications with a specific purpose of use;</li>
<li>External terminology (classes and properties) used for new/additional terms that do not appear in existing vocabularies.</li>
</ul>
</p>
<p>To comply with this application profile, an implementation requires that:</p>
<p>
<ul>
<li>MUST For each class, always contain the properties that have at least cardinality 1.</li>
<li>MAY NOT contain more than 1 instance of properties with 1 as maximum cardinality.</li>
<li>MAY use terminology (classes and properties) in a way consistent with its semantics (definition, usage, domain, and scope).</li>
<li>MAY NOT use terminology from other controlled vocabularies than that defined in this application profile.</li>
<li>MAG can be extended with classes and properties from other data models (vocabularia) that do not overlap with terminology from this application profile.</li>
</ul>
</p>  
{% endblock %}

